    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "The Stanford Study of Writing is a landmark longitudinal study of college writers and college writing. Active between Fall 2001 and Spring 2006 at Stanford University, the SSW followed 189 members of the Class of 2005 through their 4 years of college and 1 year beyond, collecting annual survey data along with writing that participants chose to share. Project researchers also conducted annual interviews with a volunteer sub-group of 38 participants. The resulting data offer a unique slice of college writing writ large from a cohort that matriculated in the weeks immediately following the terrorist attacks of 9/11 and concluded their first post-graduate year as Facebook opened to general users from around the world. \r\n\r\nIn total, 186 participants contributed the 13, 086 files included in this data set. At time of submission, all text files were converted to plain text (.txt), and in some cases non-ASCII characters were replaced with question marks.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
